<title>SWITZERLAND: Fourth Swiss beet test shows higher beet weight.</title>
<headline>Fourth Swiss beet test shows higher beet weight.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Switzerland's fourth sugar beet test showed a higher average beet weight and sugar content than last year, Zuckerfabrik + Raffinerie Aarberg AG said.</p>
<p>The test was carried out on September 10. Details follow:</p>
<p>				 4th test 96   4th test 95   3rd test 96</p>
<p> Beet weight, grammes	  961	     758	     898</p>
<p> Beets per hectare, tonnes   87.1	    67.6	    81.6</p>
<p> Leaf-root weight ratio	0.7	     0.6	     0.8</p>
<p> Sugar content, percent	17.5	    15.9	    15.1</p>
<p> Rain since April 1 (mm)     388.9	   438.8	   379.7</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
